    "caveat": "A household survey, not a price list, and eight years old. Every figure is an average over a stratum -- a state, a sector, an ailment category -- and the report publishes no quantile of the patient-level distribution, so a band fitted to these cells describes the spread of average cost across strata and not the spread across patients. The public-hospital column is out-of-pocket spending at a government hospital, which is neither the CGHS rate nor the PM-JAY package price. Figures are July 2017 - June 2018 rupees and exclude hospitalisation for childbirth, transport to hospital, and food.",
